  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered"><span class="username">Chamilka</span>, You Are The <span class="archetype">Sage</span> - <span class="text-orange">And This Is What It Means...</span></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/it-means.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>The Sage is highly dedicated when it comes to seeking two things: knowledge and wisdom. That's what forms the foundation of the Sage archetype - it's what it lives for, and what it thrives on.</p>
              <p>Practically everything that you experience in life is a lesson for you, as you're able to identify the obscure meanings behind every event, occurrence, and setback.</p>
              <p>Truth be told, <span class="text-orange">the Sage archetype is not merely one-dimensional</span>. It has many different sides and faces, and as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction, you'll begin to understand what I mean. But before we proceed, please do so with with an open mind, and a willing heart.</p>
              <p><span class="username"></span> the Sage archetype is the wisest of all the archetypes. Your inherent wisdom is derived from your acute observations, and vast experiences of the world.</p>
              <p>This inner sense of wisdom is motivated by your curiosity of everything that life has to offer - its experiences and philosophies. To you, life in itself is a lifelong lesson; one that has no ceremonies or graduations - rather, a perpetual cycle of learning.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>But what really sets you apart is your <span class="text-orange">wonder for Truth</span>. You’re deeply intuitive and introspective, and you're constantly applying and enriching yourself throughout the course of your life. You keep your principles and values close to your heart, and you're an advocate of mutual respect, peace, and harmony.</p>
          <p>Although you have the desire to attain knowledge, there are instances where you prefer to listen to your own intuition.</p>
          <p>Add to that, you have a profound understanding of the world, and there is a unique part that exists within you... A part that believes that intuitive thinking is often more reliable than logic processing.</p>
          <p>It's more than likely that you are an individual who has a deep interest in the spiritual world - an intangible dimension that exists beneath the layer of life.</p>
          <p>Others find themselves drawn to you because of your <span class="text-orange">wisdom, insights, and prudence</span>. This translates into your behavior in front of others, as your words are carefully selected.</p>
          <p>Needless to say, the Sage is representative of a progressive world, and an enlightened life.</p>
          <p><span class="username"></span>, you are certainly not one to be motivated by material possessions. You're far more interested in discovering the way to attaining inner peace.</p>
          <p>That typically stems from the realization that life is short-lived, and possessions are merely temporary.</p>
          <p>You are also an individual who enjoys reading - whether it comes in the form of books, articles, or newspapers. You're not typically interested in a single subject, but you enjoy reading things of different genres, natures, and mediums.</p>
          <p><span class="text-orange">Your curiosity is what contributes to your vast pool of knowledge</span>, but that is not what ultimately defines you as a Sage.</p>
          <p>What really sets the Sage apart from the rest of the archetypes is its dedication to a higher sense of self - a journey of discovering experiences, and living life at a level beyond the comprehension of others.</p>
          <p>But we'll discuss that in greater detail as we progress through this Archetypal Introduction, <span class="username"></span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Sage</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Qualities, Unknown Tendencies,<br>And Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As a person of philosophical nature, you tend to be quite introverted. It isn’t that you don’t prefer company at all, but this does mean that you tend to need time away from people in order to concentrate on your ideas. The more time you spend away from others, the more you are able to refine them, which in turn betters both yours and other people’s lives.</p>
              <p>Sages tend to be quite egocentric, which means that you look after your needs before that of other people. And while this is a perfectly valid and even understandable impulse, the problem is that you can sometimes end up trampling on other people in the process, as <span class="text-orange">selfishness gives way to pride and bouts of supremacy</span>.</p>
              <p>Aside from egocentrism, you are also rational, preferring to fight problems with your head rather than your heart. Needless to say, this means that you have a refined mindset when solving problems, as you tend to see everything as puzzles that need solving. From time to time, however, this can give way to false interpretations about you, considering that you do tend to set emotions aside.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>More importantly, calmness is necessary for philosophical thought, and in your case, you have much of it. Your desire to have a steady mind is often rewarded with a clear understanding of everything around you and a set of friends who idolize this side of you. On the other hand, it could make it appear as though you don’t take situations too seriously, or perhaps that you don’t even care.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>. With your hidden qualities in full view, it is time for you to know what your strengths are and how you can better use them...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-1" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(1,2)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Sage, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As a Sage, your mind has an eye of its own that allows it to see reality in multiple different ways. Where most may not see the drawbacks of something that seems good on the surface, you know better-- and vice versa.</p>
              <p>This can function on multiple levels. On an individual scale, you are able to grasp certain implications in the things you read, for example, that most people might miss. This can include references or subtle lessons that, when applied in reality, can make a difference in your life, improving your decision-making.</p>
              <p>Your wide-mindedness also has a social dimension. While you may not communicate with people yourself, you can see hints of agitation in one’s body language or the general context you are in. As such, <span class="text-orange">you often have insights that could potentially end conflicts within groups</span>.</p>
              <p>The line between the truth and emotion can be extremely fragile, and it only gets worse the more complicated a situation becomes. In this regard, the strength of the Sage lies in their ability to full separate the two, giving them an enormous advantage in life.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>For example, they are more likely to get to the heart of any conflict than most archetypes. Since they can think beyond their feelings-- or that of others-- they can cleave to the issue at hand and call out both sides for it, to the point where compromises can be reached.</p>
          <p>This also highly contributes to the Sage’s intellect. They are <span class="text-orange">capable of detecting even their own personal biases</span> when reading into details and are often quick to purge or at least put them in the back burner for later, enhancing their capacity for research and even teamwork.</p>
          <p>Add to that, rationality is the Sage’s foremost weapon, and in this regard, you have much to offer. More than just the ability to break things down into parts, you also have a critical mind that regularly asks questions.</p>
          <p>This manifests more precisely in moments where you are in <span class="text-orange">deep thought</span>. When you need to consider multiple perspectives, you often ask questions that can seem contradictory to your own beliefs. You aren’t afraid to challenge yourself to think beyond the box of your own beliefs or ideologies.</p>
          <p>Even better, however, is the fact that you aren’t afraid to use this ability for other people. When they assert themselves and become emotional, you are able to take a step back and tell them what they did wrong and how they can improve it. Thus, you are more than capable of giving advice.</p>
          <p>As complete thinkers, Sages don’t just take into account the circumstances around them and make deductions based on all available information. They are also highly capable of actually making the leap from thought to decision. They may have their <span class="text-orange">moments of hesitation</span>, but only when they aren’t presented the full context.</p>
          <p>Thus, you are more than capable of making decisions not just for yourself but also for a group of people under or with you. This naturally translates to a more straightforward career and financial path on the individual level, as you are able to make informed decisions and execute them without much hesitation. </p>
          <p>What's more is the fact that this means you are also a capable leader when pushed into the role. You may not be so inclined to do so due to having a more introverted mindset, but because you are also wise, you know that sometimes, your individual needs will have to be sacrificed or set aside for the greater good. As such, you are able to deliver and step up when it truly matters.</p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life. </p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Sage, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your rational nature, you tend to believe in the supremacy of logic. Whereas other archetypes tend to be passionate and forgiving, you are inclined to follow your inner logician over your own partner.</p>
              <p>When you are in a relationship, this tendency will bring heated discussion. As such, your relationship may be somewhat fragile on a daily basis. When important matters are actually happening, you will likely have your own opinions, and the pushback could be just as severe depending on your partner.</p>
              <p>Given this, you are likely to look for a partner who can handle this assertiveness. In the process, you may have multiple partners as you try to find the right one and suffer communication failures along the way.</p>
              <p>Of course, assertiveness isn’t always a bad thing. <span class="text-orange">Planting your feet on the ground and being stubborn when it counts</span> will make your partner feel like they are standing with an equal. Under the right circumstances, assertiveness is competence in action-- and the outcome that vindicates it is proof that it can work.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Assertiveness also gives the impression of righteous confidence in a relationship. Knowing that you are able to steer the wheel can be a reassuring thought for when emergencies happen.</p>
          <p>However, that being said, too much of it can also give off the wrong impression that a relationship is dictatorial. When this happens, it might only enhance miscommunication between the two of you. In the long term, this could be fatal to the relationship itself as either you or your partner might become fed up.</p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Thus, you should focus on keeping your <span class="text-orange">assertiveness at reasonable levels</span>. Argue your case if you must, but you have to be open to concessions or alternatives, as these might be better than your own. Not being overly assertive also promotes equality in a relationship and keeps it going for long.</p>
          <p>Looking at the core qualities of your archetype, we’ll see a Sage who wants nothing more than certainty. Even in romance, Sages can take time to process their feelings as they often ruminate on what it means for them.</p>
          <p>This trait often manifests in your likelihood to stop and think about your relationship first. You’ll likely not put labels on relationships until you are absolutely sure that what you feel for the person is true love.</p>
          <p>This trait is consistent with your own cautious introversion. You might behave like this in romantic contexts because when a Sage falls in love, it means they are <span class="text-orange">inviting someone into their own introverted world</span>. Everything about a Sage’s individuality matters, so you would not want to waste that on a partner who would not last.</p>
          <p>Consequently, if you do end up exploring and finding partners, you will likely tell them to keep the relationship private or not designate it as anything, because you want to feel them out.</p>
          <p>However, this trait can also create the impression that you are leading your romantic partner on. You may tell them to court you for extended periods of time and wait, and during the process, there is a chance that your doubts might become a <span class="text-orange">self-fulfilling prophecy</span> you might not have the love of your life because you insist on waiting and taking your time.</p>
          <p>Of course, regardless of the outcome, none of this is fundamentally wrong. It’s okay to doubt, more than anything, in order to secure a good relationship. But there is such a thing as too much doubting, and Sages are encouraged to loosen up a bit and let the world do its magic.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Sage is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>.</p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Sage</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Sage is a combination of introversion, egocentrism, rationality, and calmness. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to the sciences, academe, and the humanities. With their wise nature, Sages have a profound ability to understand the world. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them. </p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/researcher.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Researcher</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Sages are best suited as researchers. Because they have the natural knack to find the truth, they’ll find it natural to be in a field that allows them to make the most of their talents.</p>
              <p>Due to your affinity for the truth, research work is your true cup of tea in many ways. There are many kinds of researchers. You can become a researcher for a private corporation, a non-profit organization or even a university of your choice!</p>
              <p>If you intend to pursue a career in the private sector, then you’ll likely land in a company that has some scientific application in mind. You may be asked to help create medicine or study digital strategies to help grow your company. You may also be placed on apprenticeships with other senior researchers or bosses to help you along the way.</p>
              <p>You can also be a researcher for non-profit organizations. These organizations will typically be researching for a cause, such as hard-to-cure diseases like Alzheimer’s disease, or even create economic approaches to help better the community. You may also try becoming a researcher for local politicians or activists who may have something new to bring to your society.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Lastly, you can go and work as a researcher in your university. This is a particularly great job to consider if you have no inclination to teach, although it is possible for you to teach while being given research grants. Depending on the caliber of your work, you will not only receive acclaim, but even actual high-paying salaries. This is also the ultimate avenue for you to pursue knowledge for knowledge’s sake, without being beholden to nearly anyone.</p>
          <p>As you can see, these jobs all have one thing in common: they give you much autonomy relative to your own job description. For example, if you choose to do research for a specific discipline in your university, you will be given free leeway to pursue what you want to study. Many professors-- Sages-- will say that there’s no limit to the adventure-- and there certainly isn’t.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/scientist.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Scientist</h5>
              <p>Sages are experts in acquiring knowledge and would do anything to be in a job that actually allows them to use such a skill to their advantage. For this reason, science is a field that comes particularly easily to them. What makes this field an even more appealing one is that there are so many areas for a Sage to focus their mind on.</p>
              <p>For example, the field of biology-- the study of life-- allows scientists to look into what truly brought us here, as well as the way in which organisms tend to work, inside and out. Knowing how we as organisms work can then translate to more practicaly applications such as how to treat diseases, achieve a longer life, or even cook our food on a daily basis. </p>
              <p>Another field, physics, concerns with objects and their general movement. The Earth is a vast expanse of land and water, so there is plenty to study on, not to mention you can also take your curiosity to space. In fact, with enough determination, you can even take your studies to space and become an astronaut!</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Aside from just studying about the earth-- or the universe for that matter-- you can also take advantage of the fact that science facilitates collaboration while allowing for significant independence. This means that you can work under some really brilliant people while actually allowing yourself to be quite free in whatever you want to study. There are plenty of routes you can take, and as a Sage, you can go for any route you want.</p>
          <p>Lastly, as a Sage, you are admittedly quite insistent on having a perfect legacy. This is something science can naturally cater to, as being able to research and being peer-reviewed will naturally create more accolades. You can have a career built upon a strong social network and even a degree of financial security that you can use to carry yourself forward.</p>
          <p>As such, if you are looking for a career that will naturally allow you to expand your mind and see what the world has to offer intellectually, science is undoubtedly the path you should take. With its many routes and opportunities for friendship and security, it will undoubtedly make you happy.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/philosophy.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Philosophy/Humanities Professor</h5>
              <p>Human beings in general have always been filled with questions, and these questions strike at the heart of what it means to be a human being in the first place: what is right and wrong? What is being? What is love? What is justice? What is fairness? These and many other questions are within the realm of philosophy-- a realm in which Sages truly feel at home.</p>
              <p>As the questions above imply, philosophy naturally appeals to the Sage’s inherent curiosity. Many of these questions may not seem all that relevant, especially to other archetypes who may be more interested in the experiences that come with life, but as you know, it is our understanding of experiences and how they are ultimately related to us that make life much more interesting.</p>
              <p>That besides, philosophy and the humanities offers you a genuine avenue to overcome overthinking. This is because generally, you’re going to be thinking about things a lot. Sometimes, you may end up either having a thought that’s completely revolutionary to your field of concentration or just overkill. The limitations that logic imposes upon you will help you refine your thoughts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>It also addresses your rudeness and elitism to a huge degree. In political theory and ethics, for example, you will learn more about your place in the world as well as how to act in front of your fellow human beings. Ultimately, you will come to understand that no human being exists in a vacuum, and that there are concepts that ultimately bind us to care for one another. Why do we do good things? Why should we be kind? These are just some of the many questions that run in these fields.</p>
          <p>With the wealth of knowledge philosophy and the humanities can offer you, professorship is certainly another route worth taking. Consider these among many others in your quest for knowledge.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-4" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(4,5)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
